1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:10,980
Louder with -af volume. Does it clip?

2
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:16,910
Nine chains, two readers.

3
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:26,960
Source: 440 Hz sine at -3 dBFS.

4
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:35,570
Two readers: astats, and raw samples.

5
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:45,870
+3 dB fits. +6 dB clips half the samples.

6
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:50,450
+12 dB clips 76.8%.

7
00:00:50,450 --> 00:01:04,300
One command: back to the source, error 0.

8
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:14,690
Two commands, 16-bit between: damage stays.

9
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:21,300
alimiter, level=disabled: peak -1 dB.

10
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:30,550
Default level: 801 samples at full scale.

11
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:37,220
Clipping happens when the file is written.

12
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:44,840
Keep gain in one chain, or use float.
